==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Nono CC''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Frolicking Nono CC''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Nono is used as a specialized meatshield against [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies. While this may seem counter-intuitive due to their generally high DPS, Nono is able to last longer than practically all other meatshields against them because of her [[Resistant|Resist]] ability. Due to her above-average recharge rate, she is essentially the anti-Dark equivalent of [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]].

Note that she has a slightly longer range than most meatshields, allowing her to form a secondary line of defense to slow down the pushing power of Dark enemies. Her range is still below [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]]'s range (240), however, so the two can work together still. This is important in stages like [[Merciless XP!|Merciless XP]] so [[Razorback]] won't randomly break through your defenses.

Unfortunately, her base health is quite lacking, so she struggles in stages that mix Dark enemies with any other trait. This weakness is most prominent in stages such as [[Gestalt, Decay]] or [[At Least I'm a Cat]]. Her cost of 315¢ is quite high as well, meaning that she will end up as a waste of money if she can't make full use of her ability.

Although she is inadvertently outclassed by a similar unit in [[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Li'l Gau]], Merc Storia returns significantly more often than Princess Punt, so she isn't off the table.

==='''True Form'''===
Nono's True Form gives her a 50% chance to Survive a lethal strike and Curse Immunity. It also reduces her backswing and increases her movement speed.

First and foremost, the speed and backswing improvements are decently useful, letting Nono frolic into the frontlines faster. Outside of that, they aren't that big of a change.

Next is her '''Survive.''' Despite this ability being on a coin-flip, due to Nono being a ranged meatshield, it can allow you to have a stronger secondary line of defense against Dark enemies. While fast-attacking enemies could easily take her out of her survived state, Nono having 190 range and most fast-attacking Dark enemies having less or equal to 190 range allows Nono to still be quite a good secondary defensive unit against them, forcing them to keep on attacking through multiple layers of Nonos slowing down their push toward your units. The Survive ability would also come in handy when you are against [[Director Kurosawah]] or [[Le'noir]] due to their slow attacks and also being Dark enemies, but despite that you shouldn't rely on her survive as much as [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] due to it having a guaranteed Survive proc and being generally better against slow-attacking enemies.

Another thing to note is Frolicking Nono's '''Curse Immunity.''' This is much more situational than her Survive ability because Curse Immune is really only useful on a unit that '''[[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|counters relics]],''' of which Nono is not. The only times this would come into play would be in Black-focused stages with the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]] or [[Loris]] like [[Cats in the Stars]] or [[Payday the 13th]].

However, the most substantial part of this True Form is the '''cost decrease'''. This unit goes from 315¢ to 285¢. While it may only lower her cost by 30¢, this means Nono is now cheaper than [[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Crystal Li'l Gau Gau]], Nono's main competition as an anti-Dark meatshield. However, this does not mean you should use this unit over him, as they still pair very well together in Dark-focused stages.

Overall, this True Form takes a good anti-Dark meatshield and makes it slightly better in terms of speed, as well as giving it a very small amount of extra utility as well as a useful cost decrease.

